  "fields": {
    "title": "Usability",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The term usability refers to the functional relationship between people and the products and systems they use. The idea is quite simple: if something is able to fulfil its intended function (if it is ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "usable",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "), then it has a good usability. Usability is a quality characteristic that evaluates the user-friendliness of user interfaces. The word also refers to methods for improving usability during the design process.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1833aR9w1g0vDYUIK0XaWp",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[1]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Jakob Nielsen, one of the best-known Human Computer Interaction (HCI) experts, argued in 2000 that users visit websites because of their content. Design, in his opinion, only fulfills the task of making content as easily accessible as possible for users. Good or successful design should be transparent in order to not disturb the content. Because websites are meant to provide information, not pleasure. Their design should be as simple and clear as possible. That is why good usability has become one of the most important points for successful design. After all, usability contributes significantly to the experience of a website. Donald Norman, who became the head of Apple's research group in 1993 and later founded the Nielsen Norman Group together with Jakob Nielsen, introduced the term Experience Design in 1993. Jakob Nielsen and Donald Norman were instrumental in coining the theory that web design, or UX design, provides the best usability, when it makes interfaces and the technology behind them invisible.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "40ON2QOZyx4NsnM0eajDYY",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[2]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "This idea can be traced back to previous developments of other focal points within the design discipline that had established themselves at the beginning of the 20th century. Styles such as Bauhaus, de Stijl or International Style had in common that they strived for a clarity of form and a kind of transparency. In his manifesto »Elementare Typography« Tschichold called for a new typography that was purposeful and clearly legible and thus as pure as possible to represent the content of the text. He also argued against any form of ornamentation and other decorative elements and called on all printed matter to standardise DIN formats. Therefore, the striving for transparency of some interface designers can be traced back to Tschichold and other modernists.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1p4tv7lu370Hv2Jih2VvOv",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "[3]",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "superscript"
                    }
                  ],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
